config BR2_PACKAGE_OPENIPC_BSEL
	bool "openipc-bsel"
	depends on BR2_arm || BR2_aarch64
	help
	  A/B bank selector for boards whose stock bootloader picks which
	  kernel/rootfs bank to boot next, so an OpenIPC image running on
	  either bank can flip which bank boots next, without the stock
	  bootloader's own userspace tool or its rootfs. Two formats, picked
	  by the partition the board has:

	  - "sel" (CADDX Ascent's "fpvboot" u-boot command): a small "BSEL"
	    magic record, reverse-engineered from the stock ar_bsel binary
	  - "gpt0"/"gpt1" (Artosyn PROXIMA 9311, BetaFPV P1): the GPT,
	    whose attribute bit 47 marks the active member of each env,
	    uboot, kernel, dtb and userapp pair for the stock SPL. It lives
	    in one of the two (primary form in gpt0, backup form in gpt1);
	    a switch writes it into the other and then erases the old one,
	    as the stock U-Boot's upgrade does

	  Installs /usr/bin/openipc-bsel, CLI-compatible with the stock tool:
	    openipc-bsel check_flash      read the bank the bootloader boots
	    openipc-bsel check_cmdline    read the running bank (fpvbsel=N,
	                                  or the userapp ubi.mtd= names)
	    openipc-bsel set 0|1          switch the next boot to bank 0/1

	  Enabled by betafpv_vr04_defconfig. Not device-specific by
	  construction: it locates the partition by name.
